Evidence A - release diff (PR #482 "catalog: group request params into a query object"):
 export function CourseList({ category, page }: Props) {
   const [courses, setCourses] = useState<Course[]>([]);
   const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
+  const query: CourseQuery = { category, page };

   useEffect(() => {
     setLoading(true);
-    fetchCourses({ category, page }).then((result) => {
+    fetchCourses(query).then((result) => {
       setCourses(result);
       setLoading(false);
     });
-  }, [category, page]);
+  }, [query]);

Evidence C - React DevTools Profiler, local reproduction (npm run dev), "Record why each component rendered" enabled:
Commit  Component    Why did this render?
41      CourseList   Hook 2 changed
42      CourseList   Hooks 1 and 2 changed
43      CourseList   Hook 2 changed
44      CourseList   Hooks 1 and 2 changed
...
CatalogPage (the parent of CourseList) did not render during the recording.
(Hook 1 = the courses state, Hook 2 = the loading state.)

Statement: "Each state update re-renders CourseList, the render creates a new query object, Object.is(previous query, new query) is false, so the effect fetches again and its response updates the state again."

